/**
 * OAuth 2.0 Device Authorization Grant (RFC 8628) for input-constrained devices.
 *
 * <p>This bounded context implements the device authorization flow, enabling devices that lack
 * a browser or have highly constrained input capabilities (smart TVs, IoT devices, CLI tools)
 * to authenticate users. The device requests a code pair from the authorization server; the user
 * enters the short user code on a secondary device with a browser; and the device polls for
 * approval. Once approved, the device exchanges the device_code for a full token set.
 *
 * <p><b>Key domain types:</b>
 * <ul>
 *   <li>{@code DeviceAuthorization} — aggregate root. Carries the device_code (long, opaque,
 *       sent to the device only), the user_code (short, human-typeable, shown to the user),
 *       the associated client_id, the requested scope set, an expiry instant, a poll interval
 *       in seconds, and the current {@code DeviceAuthorizationStatus}. Created atomically on
 *       the device authorization endpoint call and updated when the user approves or denies.</li>
 *   <li>{@code DeviceAuthorizationStatus} — enum with three states: PENDING (awaiting user
 *       action), APPROVED (user confirmed on the verification UI), DENIED (user explicitly
 *       declined or the device_code expired). The device polls until status leaves PENDING.</li>
 *   <li>{@code DeviceAuthorizationException} — domain exception encoding the RFC 8628 error
 *       responses returned to the polling device: {@code authorization_pending} (still waiting),
 *       {@code slow_down} (polled too fast), {@code access_denied} (user denied),
 *       {@code expired_token} (device_code TTL exceeded).</li>
 *   <li>{@code DeviceAuthorizationGateway} — primary outbound port. Provides:
 *       {@code store} a new {@code DeviceAuthorization}, {@code findByDeviceCode} for polling
 *       and token exchange, {@code findByUserCode} for the user verification UI to display the
 *       associated client and scope, and {@code updateStatus} for the approval/denial action.</li>
 * </ul>
 *
 * <p><b>Key application services:</b>
 * <ul>
 *   <li>{@code DeviceAuthorizationService} — orchestrates three operations:
 *       (1) {@code authorize}: validates the client, generates the device_code and user_code
 *       pair, stores the record, and returns the endpoint response (device_code, user_code,
 *       verification_uri, verification_uri_complete, expires_in, interval).
 *       (2) {@code pollStatus}: loads the record by device_code, enforces the poll-interval
 *       rate limit (slow_down), and returns the current status or throws the RFC 8628 error.
 *       (3) {@code approve} / {@code deny}: called by the user-verification HTML controller
 *       after the user confirms or rejects, transitioning the status accordingly.</li>
 * </ul>
 *
 * <p><b>Infrastructure adapters:</b>
 * <ul>
 *   <li>{@code DeviceAuthorizationSqlAdapter} — driven SQL adapter implementing
 *       {@code DeviceAuthorizationGateway}. Persists device authorization records with TTL-based
 *       expiry and handles the atomic status-update operation.</li>
 *   <li>{@code DeviceVerificationHtml} — HTML driver rendering the user-facing verification page
 *       (GET /device, POST /device/approve, POST /device/deny). Loads the pending authorization
 *       by user_code, shows client name and requested scopes, and triggers approval/denial.</li>
 *   <li>{@code DevicesAccessController} (in Authentication context) — REST driver handling the
 *       POST /device_authorization endpoint and the device_code token-exchange grant type at
 *       the token endpoint, bridging the Device context and the Authentication granter.</li>
 * </ul>
 *
 * <p><b>Internal structure:</b>
 * <pre>
 * device/
 * ├── domain/
 * │   ├── DeviceAuthorization.java      — aggregate root (device_code, user_code, status)
 * │   ├── DeviceAuthorizationStatus.java — PENDING / APPROVED / DENIED enum
 * │   ├── exception/DeviceAuthorizationException.java — RFC 8628 error enum
 * │   └── gateway/DeviceAuthorizationGateway.java
 * ├── application/
 * │   └── DeviceAuthorizationService.java
 * └── infrastructure/
 *     ├── driven/DeviceAuthorizationSqlAdapter.java
 *     └── driver/html/DeviceVerificationHtml.java
 * </pre>
 *
 * <p><b>Dependencies:</b> Client context (client validation at authorization time). The token
 * endpoint for device_code exchange is in the Authentication context
 * ({@code DevicesAccessController}). No direct dependency on Session context (device flow uses
 * its own polling mechanism rather than a browser session cookie).
 *
 * <p><b>Stability:</b> partially implemented; RFC 8628 defines the protocol precisely but the
 * poll-rate enforcement, user_code display customization, and PKCE support for device flow are
 * areas of pending work.
 */
